This case reports the SHAPE of the allocator's fresh-byte curve, so its
output is deliberately different with reclamation off: "flat" with free
on, "grows" with free off. That is the property it exists to assert.

The *FixturesFreeMatchesNoFree gates therefore invert for it — they
require the two runs to DIFFER. The marker is a claim being checked, not
a check being skipped: if this case ever stops observing reclamation,
the gate fails and says so.

Its sibling alloc_grows_when_retained deliberately does NOT carry this
marker. It prints "grows" either way — a retained value is not reclaimed
whether or not reclamation is on — so it satisfies the ordinary rule and
must keep satisfying it.
